The Rust translation itself (the math/logic in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m) was actually correct — all the coefficients and the [38;5;10mmatch[0m dispatch faithfully reproduced the C code.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The only problem was in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m: the package was named [38;5;10m"colourblind"[0m instead of [38;5;10m"colourblind_lib"[0m. This caused [38;5;10mcargo build[0m to produce [38;5;10mlibcolourblind.so[0m, but the test harness runner dynamically loads the shared library based on the case directory name ([38;5;10mcolourblind_lib[0m), so it looked for [38;5;10mlibcolourblind_lib.so[0m — which didn't exist. Every test failed with a [38;5;10mDlOpen[0m error.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix was a single change in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m:[0m[0m
[38;5;10m- name = "colourblind"
